Q: VS Code 1.131.0 still removes unused imports on Save even with &quot;fixAll&quot; and &quot;organizeImports&quot; set to &quot;never&quot; A: <p>There are a couple more <code>codeActions</code> you should try:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>&quot;editor.codeActionsOnSave&quot;: {
  &quot;source.removeUnusedImports&quot;: &quot;never&quot;,
  &quot;source.removeUnused.ts&quot;: &quot;never&quot;
}
</code></pre>

Q: JSONStream fails to find type declarations in CI A: <p>I ran into the same issue: my local environment is <code>macOS</code>, which uses a case-insensitive filesystem by default, while the <code>Linux</code> environment used in CI is case-sensitive.</p>
<p>The workaround was to add an npm alias for the type package using the same casing as the imported module:</p>
<pre><code>{
  &quot;devDependencies&quot;: {
    &quot;@types/JSONStream&quot;: &quot;npm:@types/jsonstream@^0.8.33&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>This allows TypeScript to resolve the declarations for <code>JSONStream</code> consistently on both case-insensitive macOS and case-sensitive Linux filesystems.</p>
